<title>MAURITIUS: U.S. firm wins phone tender in Mauritius.</title>
<headline>U.S. firm wins phone tender in Mauritius.</headline>
<dateline>PORT LOUIS 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. company Qualcomm Corp has won a tender to install 50,000 wireless local loop (WLL) telephone lines in the Indian Ocean island of Mauritius, a senior (Mauritius) Central Tender Board official said.</p>
<p>The official said Qualcomm bid 1.1 billion rupees ($53.89 million) for the project, ahead of fellow American company Motorola Inc. He would not say what Motorola's bid was.</p>
